files.why:
Twelve new routing rows: full-run-crashed, exe-runs-missing, exe-settled-missing, exe-guard-stop, cancel-guard-stop, probe-guard-stop, cancel-ran-full, boot-settles-before-i0, boot-settles-then-listing-reclaimed, boot-never-settled and settle-marks-missing. Three new Facts check the reasons:
- ExeRunsThatAreMissingCrashedOrStoppedByTheGuardNeverPass;
- TheBootSettlesBeforeI0OrTheRunDecidesNothing;
- TheNoLinkCheckCanFailAndTheProtocolRefusesWhenItDid.
The O-078 refused-paste cases (fltmc.txt, and an environment record) are added to MissingOrNullReadingsAreUndecidedAndABurstGapIsLeftOutOfDrift. The run builder writes settle marks and can set exit codes and guard stops. A shared PoolWatch() runner replaces the -Report-only helper.

obligations.how:
Get-Verdict now checks the exe runs before judging them. It returns UNDECIDED, naming the problem, when:
- the exe-full arms or the exe-cancel/exe-close arms are not exactly five each;
- any of those arms lacks its before or settled mark;
- a full run has exit != 0, no report, or report.status != Completed (unless the guard stopped it);
- a cancelled run has no report;
- a cancelled or closed run ranFull, because its trigger never fired.
OverArm makes a guard stop count as over T on L, S, P and every exe run. The rows full-run-crashed, exe-runs-missing and exe-guard-stop are in TheReportRoutesARunAsTheToleranceRowSays, with exe-settled-missing, cancel-guard-stop, probe-guard-stop and cancel-ran-full. The reviewer's measured case (F3 exit 70, no report) now gives 'UNDECIDED: full run F3 did not complete: exit 70, no report'; before, it read A/PASS. All 31 PoolWatchReportTests pass.

-Protocol now writes R0, then settle/NN marks every MarkEverySec until two gaps in a row each move both pools by less than 16 MiB (Tolerance.SettleStepBytes, spike 3's V2 rule), with a 30-minute cap (SettleCapSec). Only then does I0 start, in both sessions. If the boot never settles, it stops with a warning. R0 stays the boot-age and guard reference. -Report recomputes the settle from the marks: no settle marks gives UNDECIDED; not settled gives VOID with the last gap's MiB. Post-pressure is now judged from L/before, because R0 now comes before the boot's settle. The tolerance row text says all of this. Evidence:
- rows boot-settles-before-i0 (1 GiB of settle over 12 gaps reads A, I0 drift about 0), boot-settles-then-listing-reclaimed (A), boot-never-settled (VOID) and settle-marks-missing (UNDECIDED);
- -Protocol -Smoke wrote R0, settle/00, settle/01, settle/02, then I0/00.

The check no longer runs its own robocopy line with /LEV:2. Test-NoLinkWalker runs through Invoke-NoLinkWalk and the shared $NoLinkFlags, which the session-2 walk now uses too. It covers:
- a planted 'All Users' junction, plus a directory symlink where one can be made: the walker must count only the root's own 10 bytes and list no 'All Users\Microsoft' at /LEV:3;
- a positive control without /XJ, which must see through the link;
- the real C:\Users at /LEV:3, with every other child excluded by /XD, so no profile is listed: no 'All Users\Microsoft'.
Measured: pwsh and 5.1 both give skips=true, though 5.1 cannot make the symlink. A scratch copy with /XJ removed gives plantedBytes 2010, usersAllUsersSkipped false, skips false, so the check can fail. -Prepare records noLinkCheck and noLinkWalkerSkipsAllUsers in smoke and real runs. -Protocol refuses to start, before taking any mark, unless that value is true. Pinned by TheNoLinkCheckCanFailAndTheProtocolRefusesWhenItDid.
